# RONDB-1124, testCteProtocol case PK-4c: a success JOIN_AGG_FINAL_REP
# that parks on a node whose SETUP has not run, and that the 200 ms
# placeholder sweeper then expires, is answered with an error FINAL_REP
# (1274), so the sender aborts and its COMPLETE fails with the temporary
# 1274 instead of waiting at the FINAL_REP barrier until DBTC times out.
# The program is the receiving node's coordinator and sends its SETUP only
# after the sweep; that late SETUP must create a fresh state.  FINAL_REP
# goes between data nodes only, so the case needs two; suite ndb_push_agg
# runs the whole program on one data node, where PK-4c is skipped.  Needs
# the leak-check DUMPs 2361 / 2362 / 2363, which crash a node on a leak;
# the program prints PASSED or FAILED.
--source include/have_ndb.inc
--source include/have_debug.inc
--source include/have_ndb_debug.inc

--echo Running testCteProtocol PK-4c (multi-node)
--exec $NDB_PUSH_AGG_DIR/testCteProtocol -c "$NDB_CONNECTSTRING" -m $MASTER_MYPORT -n PK-4c
